update programs set intro = replace(intro, 'Last Seat is Elite-only and expensive, and is available whenever seats remain on the flight, per current program rules.', 'Last Seat is Elite-only and expensive, and is generally available when unsold seats remain on the flight - though Frontier reserves the right to limit inventory per current program rules.'), last_verified = current_date where slug = 'frontier' and intro like '%Last Seat is Elite-only and expensive, and is available whenever seats remain on the flight, per current program rules.%';

-- [MEDIUM] how_to_spend: Same issue as intro: presents Last Seat availability as a certainty ('available whenever seats remain') when the program's own T&C says it is not guaranteed.
update programs set how_to_spend = replace(how_to_spend, 'Last Seat (Elite-only, most miles, available whenever seats remain per current program rules)', 'Last Seat (Elite-only, most miles, generally available when seats remain - not guaranteed per current program rules)'), last_verified = current_date where slug = 'frontier' and how_to_spend like '%Last Seat (Elite-only, most miles, available whenever seats remain per current program rules)%';

-- [MEDIUM] quirks: A co-brand card is presented as an active option without confirming it is currently issuable to new applicants — it is only accessible via 'targeted offers,' which means it may be effectively discontinued or unavailable to most readers; it should be explicitly labeled as not publicly available rather than presented as a parallel active product.
update programs set quirks = replace(quirks, '**Frontier Airlines Business Mastercard** also exists alongside the consumer World Mastercard - both are Barclays-issued. The Business card is offered through special targeted offers rather than a permanent public application page; if you''re a small-business owner who flies Frontier regularly, watch the Barclays cards page or status-match-style offers.', '**Frontier Airlines Business Mastercard (not publicly available)** - a Barclays-issued business co-brand card has existed but is not offered through a permanent public application page. It surfaces only through targeted offers. Do not rely on this card being available; include it only if you receive a direct targeted offer.'), last_verified = current_date where slug = 'frontier' and quirks like '%**Frontier Airlines Business Mastercard** also exists alongside the consumer World Mastercard - both are Barclays-issued. The Business card is offered through special targeted offers rather than a permanent public application page; if you''re a small-business owner who flies Frontier regularly, watch the Barclays cards page or status-match-style offers.%';

